                <pb facs="0242" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1946v03/pg198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">CFM Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Journal</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-chapter-heading" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1946-08-13T21:30:00+01:00">August 13, 1946, 9:30 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">USDel (PC) (Journal) 15</p>
                <p>Mr. Dunn (U.S.) said that his delegation considered it inadvisable for a
                    representative of any state which prepared the draft peace treaties to be chosen
                    as <hi rendition="#italic">rapporteur</hi> of any of the commissions. Mr.
                    Vyshinsky (U.S.S.R.) disagreed with Mr. Dunn’s view. Mr. Egeland (South Africa)
                    was nominated for Chairman of the Commission by M. Vyshinsky and seconded by Dr.
                    Evatt (Australia). He was unanimously elected. Mr. McNeil (U.K.) proposed M.
                    Manouilsky (Ukraine) as Vice Chairman and he was unanimously elected by
                    acclamation. The election of a <hi rendition="#italic">rapporteur</hi> was
                    postponed until the next meeting.</p>
            </div>
